# Copy this file to `.kamal/secrets` before the first deploy.
#
#     cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets
#
# `.kamal/secrets` is in .gitignore. This example isn't: it contains no
# secret, it just says where to get them.
#
# No registry token is needed. The registry is local: Kamal spins up a
# `registry:3` on this machine and opens a reverse SSH port-forward so the
# NAS can pull from its own localhost. With a server that starts with
# "localhost", Kamal doesn't even try to do a `docker login`.
#
# The master key lives in config/master.key, which is also gitignored. If
# you cloned the repo onto a new machine, copy it from one that already has
# it: without it, the app won't boot in production.
RAILS_MASTER_KEY=$(cat config/master.key)
